- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignNamesakeCount.java:12, 24` (computes and sets it)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java:24` (read in the tier expression)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml:2104` (schema field)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java:85` (comment)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java:16` (comment "namesake0")

`membershipLevel` (the new numeric field the tests expect, not yet in main)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java:7, 16`

---

### 2. The tier computation logic

There are **two layers**:

**(a) SILVER / BRONZE — MapStruct expression** in `OwnerMapper.java:24`:
```java
@Mapping(target = "membershipTier", expression = "java(java.lang.Integer.valueOf(0).equals(owner.getNamesakeCount()) && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty() ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\")")
```
So `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` AND email present; otherwise `BRONZE`.

**(b) GOLD override** — `HouseholdTier` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/HouseholdTier.java`), full class:
```java
public final class HouseholdTier {
    private HouseholdTier() {}

    /** True when the owner belongs to a household of three or more members. */
    public static boolean isGold(Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        String householdId = owner.getHouseholdId();
        if (householdId == null) {
            return false;
        }
        int members = 0;
        for (Owner other : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (householdId.equals(other.getHouseholdId())) {
                members++;
            }
        }
        return members >= 3;
    }
}
```

**`namesakeCount` producer** — `AssignNamesakeCount` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/AssignNamesakeCount.java`), full `service` method:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String firstName = normalize(owner.getFirstName());
    String lastName = normalize(owner.getLastName());
    int count = 0;
    for (Owner other : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (firstName.equals(normalize(other.getFirstName()))
                && lastName.equals(normalize(other.getLastName()))) {
            count++;
        }
    }
    owner.setNamesakeCount(count);
}
private static String normalize(String value) {
    return value == null ? "" : value.trim().toLowerCase();
}
```

---

### 3. Response DTO with `membershipTier`

There is no hand-written `OwnerDto`; it is **generated from the OpenAPI spec**. The `membershipTier` property is defined in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml:2112-2117`:
```yaml
membershipTier:
  title: Membership tier
  description: "'SILVER' when namesakeCount is 0 and an email is present, otherwise 'BRONZE'."
  type: string
  example: 'SILVER'
  readOnly: true
```
The generated `OwnerDto.setMembershipTier(String)` is called in both response functions:
- `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java:19` (create flow)
- `RespondWithOwner.java:16` (read flow)

Both do: map via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` (sets SILVER/BRONZE), then override to `"GOLD"` if `HouseholdTier.isGold(...)`.

---

### 4. Audit logging around record creation

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` — full class:
```java
public class AuditOwnerCreated {
